source: crates/fauxfield/tests/cli.rs
expression: out
---
Local-first mock API tool: desktop app, headless runner, CLI and MCP server.

Usage: fauxfield [OPTIONS] [PATH]
       fauxfield <COMMAND>

Commands:
  open         Open the desktop app, optionally on a workspace folder
  init         Create a workspace (SPEC §4.1) with one example server
  validate     Validate the workspace files; exit code 3 when there are errors
  workspace    Show or rename the workspace
  server       List and inspect Servers
  route        List and inspect Routes
  response     Add and configure Responses of a Route
  env          List, switch and add Environments
  var          Get, set and unset variables at a scope
  callback     Fire the Callbacks (webhooks) of a recorded request again
  ws           List WebSocket connections, read the timeline, send messages, disconnect clients
  data         List, show, reset, export and import Datasets
  certs        Show, trust and untrust the development CA used by HTTPS Servers
  doctor       Check ports, the development CA trust state and certificate expiry
  render       Render a Response template against a sample request, without running a server
  run          Serve a workspace headless: become the host and run its servers until stopped
  status       Show the running host and its servers (exit code 4 when no host is running)
  stop         Stop servers on the running host; without --server also ends a headless host
  logs         Print request logs from the running host
  mcp          Run the MCP server for agents (SPEC §11.1). Logs go to stderr; stdout is protocol-only
  agents       Set up coding agents (MCP client config, AGENTS.md)
  theme        List and choose the color theme
  record       Record traffic from an upstream into a Server (arrives in M12)
  import       Import an OpenAPI document (arrives in M15)
  export       Export an OpenAPI document (arrives in M15)
  template     List and apply Templates (arrives in M15)
  version      Print version information
  completions  Print a shell completion script to stdout
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [PATH]  Workspace folder to open (default: the nearest ancestor containing fauxfield.toml)

Options:
  -q, --quiet     Suppress informational output
      --no-color  Disable coloured output (also honoured: the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -h, --help      Print help
  -V, --version   Print version
